@startuml
autonumber
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam backgroundcolor white
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

title UML Sequence Diagram (v2) – Main System Workflow\nBlockchain-Enabled IoT System for Produce Traceability and Cold Chain Monitoring

actor "Supply Chain Operator" as Operator
participant "Web Dashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Backend System" as Backend
participant "IoT Device (ESP32 + DHT22)" as IoT
database "Database" as DB
participant "Blockchain Network" as Blockchain

== 1. LOGIN ==
Operator -> Dashboard: Enter login credentials
Dashboard -> Backend: Submit credentials
Backend -> DB: Verify user (password hash)
DB --> Backend: Authentication result
alt Valid credentials
    Backend --> Dashboard: Return access token (role claim)
    Dashboard --> Operator: Display dashboard
else Invalid credentials
    Backend --> Dashboard: Login error
    Dashboard --> Operator: Login failed
end

== 2. PRODUCE BATCH REGISTRATION AND DEVICE ASSIGNMENT ==
Operator -> Dashboard: Enter produce batch details
Dashboard -> Backend: Submit batch details (token)
Backend -> DB: Store batch and traceability record
DB --> Backend: Return Batch ID
Backend --> Dashboard: Return QR identifier / QR code
Dashboard --> Operator: Display QR code
Backend -> Blockchain: Submit BATCH_REGISTERED hash (asynchronous, see 6)
Operator -> Dashboard: Attach IoT device to batch
Dashboard -> Backend: Create device assignment
Backend -> DB: Store DEVICE_ASSIGNMENT (one active per device)

== 3. IOT ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING ==
IoT -> Backend: Send reading + device API key\n(Temperature, Humidity, Timestamp, Device ID)
Backend -> DB: Authenticate device and validate payload
Backend -> DB: Resolve batch from active assignment
Backend -> DB: Store environmental reading
DB --> Backend: Confirm stored reading
Backend --> IoT: Acknowledge (201)
Backend -> Backend: Evaluate thresholds for produce type\n(breach / recovery counters)

== 4. ENVIRONMENTAL ALERT (EXCURSION) ==
alt Excursion opened or closed
    Backend -> DB: Record ALERT and COLD_CHAIN_EVENT
    Backend -> Dashboard: Send environmental alert
    Dashboard -> Operator: Display alert
    Operator -> Dashboard: Acknowledge alert
    Dashboard -> Backend: Acknowledge
    Backend -> DB: Update alert status
else Within threshold or excursion already open
    Backend -> Backend: Continue monitoring (no new event)
end

== 5. COLD-CHAIN / MOVEMENT EVENT ==
Operator -> Dashboard: Record cold-chain event or produce movement
Dashboard -> Backend: Submit event details (token)
Backend -> DB: Store event / movement record
DB --> Backend: Confirm record

== 6. BLOCKCHAIN ANCHORING (EVENTS ONLY – NEVER RAW READINGS) ==
Backend -> DB: Create BLOCKCHAIN_RECORD (PENDING, canonical payload hash)
Backend -> Blockchain: Submit record hash
alt Transaction confirmed
    Blockchain --> Backend: Return transaction hash / confirmation
    Backend -> DB: Store blockchain reference (CONFIRMED)
else Failure or timeout
    Backend -> DB: Mark FAILED and schedule retry
end

== 7. VIEW MONITORING AND TRACEABILITY INFORMATION ==
Operator -> Dashboard: Request monitoring/traceability information
Dashboard -> Backend: Request records (token)
Backend -> DB: Retrieve environmental, batch and traceability records
DB --> Backend: Return records
Backend --> Dashboard: Return monitoring and traceability information
Dashboard --> Operator: Display dashboard and traceability information

== 8. INTEGRITY VERIFICATION ==
Operator -> Dashboard: Verify record
Dashboard -> Backend: Request verification
Backend -> DB: Retrieve record and stored hash reference
Backend -> Backend: Recompute canonical hash
Backend -> Blockchain: Read anchored hash by transaction reference
Blockchain --> Backend: Return anchored hash
Backend --> Dashboard: Verified / Tampered
Dashboard --> Operator: Display verification result

caption Figure 6 (v2): UML Sequence Diagram – Main System Workflow
@enduml
